1vk8|v|To cause to move with quick or violent vibrations; to move rapidly one way and the other; to make to tremble or shiver; to agitate. ; Fig.: To move from firmness; to weaken the stability of; to cause to waver; to impair the resolution of. ; To give a tremulous tone to; to trill; as, to shake a note in music. ; To move or remove by agitating; to throw off by a jolting or vibrating motion; to rid one's self of; -- generally with an adverb, as off, out, etc.; as, to shake fruit down from a tree. ; To be agitated with a waving or vibratory motion; to tremble; to shiver; to quake; to totter.	o:xfe,103,5~xfe,103,5
1vle|n|of Shame	a:1o03,91,6~1o03,91,6
1vm5|n|To form or create; especially, to mold or make into a particular form; to give proper form or figure to. ; To adapt to a purpose; to regulate; to adjust; to direct; as, to shape the course of a vessel. ; To image; to conceive; to body forth. ; To design; to prepare; to plan; to arrange. ; Character or construction of a thing as determining its external appearance; outward aspect; make; figure; form; guise; as, the shape of a tree; the shape of the head; an elegant shape. ; That which has form or figure; a figure; an appearance; a being. ; A model; a pattern; a mold. ; Form of embodiment, as in words; form, as of thought or conception; concrete embodiment or example, as of some quality. ; Dress for disguise; guise. ; A rolled or hammered piece, as a bar, beam, angle iron, etc., having a cross section different from merchant bar. ; A piece which has been roughly forged nearly to the form it will receive when completely forged or fitted.	a:f6m,82,3;142z,80,5;hsa,65,3;1q11,65,4;huw,62,2;26ek,54,3;jry,51,6;ekr,51,8;1slb,43,3;1g8t,37,4;1g10,36,4;6lh,34,4;1y56,27,13;1is1,25,2;v56,18,5~1y56,27,13;w2z,8,10;1tcb,9,8;kgh,11,8;ekr,51,8;jry,51,6;7km,11,6;1mx7,14,5;v56,18,5;142z,80,5;1g10,36,4;6lh,34,4;1q11,65,4;1g8t,37,4;g7a,14,3	v:c2v,11,4;y2j,2,3~c2v,11,4;y2j,2,3	n:1qat,66,2;eyg,64,3;hsa,49,1;26ek,48,2;hus,45,4;mux,43,5;1smd,38,2;1xwa,28,6;aee,21,2;gwe,17,3;237u,14,3;6wc,13,13~6wc,13,13;1xwa,28,6;mux,43,5;hus,45,4;eyg,64,3;gwe,17,3;237u,14,3;1qat,66,2;1smd,38,2;aee,21,2;26ek,48,2;hsa,49,1	N:v5s,60,2~v5s,60,2
