1vmj|n|The part (usually an iron or steel plate) of a plow which cuts the ground at the bottom of a furrow; a plowshare. ; The part which opens the ground for the reception of the seed, in a machine for sowing seed.	a:ri1,46,10~ri1,46,10	v:1kpt,20,10;aox,5,2~1kpt,20,10;aox,5,2	n:1933,39,3;1kpt,36,31;5pe,30,9;3tm,12,3;aox,5,2~1kpt,36,31;5pe,30,9;1933,39,3;3tm,12,3;aox,5,2	N:1080,29,5;1o06,23,3;1fbx,22,1;du3,21,6;i7o,20,6;12cm,6,3;qyl,6,3;15jl,5,1;1xo2,1,5~i7o,20,6;du3,21,6;1080,29,5;1xo2,1,5;qyl,6,3;12cm,6,3;1o06,23,3;15jl,5,1;1fbx,22,1
