1vyn|n|imp. & p. p. of Shoot. ; of Shot ; The act of shooting; discharge of a firearm or other weapon which throws a missile. ; A missile weapon, particularly a ball or bullet; specifically, whatever is discharged as a projectile from firearms or cannon by the force of an explosive. ; Small globular masses of lead, of various sizes, -- used chiefly for killing game; as, bird shot; buckshot. ; The flight of a missile, or the distance which it is, or can be, thrown; as, the vessel was distant more than a cannon shot. ; A marksman; one who practices shooting; as, an exellent shot.	a:17p1,45,7;1ubz,41,1;zbk,21,1;sjm,21,4~17p1,45,7;sjm,21,4;zbk,21,1;1ubz,41,1	v:vdp,12,3~vdp,12,3	n:1ubz,79,14~1ubz,79,14
