1w15|n|The act shrinking; shrinkage; contraction; also, recoil; withdrawal.	V:25yq,85,4~25yq,85,4	n:xuk,45,7~xuk,45,7	N:rfv,60,4~rfv,60,4
1w15|v|To wrinkle, bend, or curl; to shrivel; hence, to contract into a less extent or compass; to gather together; to become compacted. ; To withdraw or retire, as from danger; to decline action from fear; to recoil, as in fear, horror, or distress. ; To express fear, horror, or pain by contracting the body, or part of it; to shudder; to quake. ; To cause to contract or shrink; as, to shrink finnel by imersing it in boiling water. ; To draw back; to withdraw.	s:19c4,53,4;xuk,37,4~xuk,37,4;19c4,53,4	D:p1c,30,3~p1c,30,3
1w16|n|The act of shrinking; a contraction into less bulk or measurement. ; The amount of such contraction; the bulk or dimension lost by shrinking, as of grain, castings, etc. ; Decrease in value; depreciation.	a:165q,56,6;ymm,38,3;1xnv,11,3~165q,56,6;1xnv,11,3;ymm,38,3	n:17w6,30,1~17w6,30,1	N:rfv,64,4~rfv,64,4
